From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: send no beacon for a link the firmware
 does not know

After a full reset, mac80211 adds the channel contexts back before the
interfaces, and mt7996_set_channel() updates the beacons of every
interface, including those not added back yet.  hostapd can also update
a beacon in that window.  The firmware then gets the beacon of a BSS it
does not know yet, and ignores the beacons it gets once the BSS is added
again: the AP sends no beacon until it is restarted.

Send the beacon of a link only once the link has been added to the
firmware.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -3540,6 +3540,10 @@ int mt7996_mcu_add_beacon(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 	if (!mlink)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* a beacon for an unknown BSS makes the firmware ignore later ones */
+	if (!(mlink->mvif->valid_links & BIT(link_conf->link_id)))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (mphy && mphy->offchannel)
 		enabled = false;
 
